      "body": "### What this fixes\n\n`ProfileMerger._discover_trace_files()` globs only `<profile_id>*.trace.json.gz`. But when a `profile_prefix` is set, `SchedulerProfilerManager._stop_profile()` writes files named:\n\n```\n<profile_prefix>-<profile_id>-TP-<rank>[-DP-...][-PP-...][-EP-...]<stage>.trace.json.gz\n```\n\nSo the trace files start with the prefix, discovery finds nothing, and `merge_profiles=True` combined with a `profile_prefix` fails with `No trace files found for profile_id`.\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd an additional `<prefix>-<profile_id>` pattern while keeping the existing one, so prefixed traces are discovered. The merged output (`merged-<profile_id>.trace.json.gz`) is still excluded by the existing filter. No API change.\n\n### Reproduction / test\n\nAdded `test_discover_trace_files_with_profile_prefix` in `test/registered/unit/utils/test_profile_merger.py`: creates `DECODE-<id>-TP-0/-TP-1` traces plus the merged output and asserts only the prefixed traces are discovered. CPU-only, no GPU needed.\n\nLocal check of the discovery logic against the new patterns (stdlib-only harness): prefixed + non-prefixed traces are found, the merged file and other profile ids are excluded.\n\n### Related / duplicate check\n\n- #20933 (same bug) was auto-closed for inactivity, and #21092 attempted it but was closed for inactivity — this revives the fix with a regression test.\n- #38914 is open and touches `_discover_trace_files`, but only to `glob.escape` literal paths; it does not add prefix discovery. This change only adds an extra pattern, so it is orthogonal.\n\n### AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used. The change is small and self-contained, and was validated with a CPU-only unit test.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35469868387](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35469868387)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35469868290](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35469868290)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35469868361](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35469868361)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
